rward generic doc, already drafted + self-reviewed for the no-secrets/no-infra requirement (grep-clean); avoiding a ~17min plan-review for a low-risk docs-only deliverable.\".","timestamp":1784045795993818001}],"created_at":1784045790868891001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"db61d5f3-11d7-4467-8c58-64d614b0280d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8d27-7ee1-f137-4b88"}],"description":"## What\n\nCreate a project-agnostic, secret-free client guide for enabling rebar's authenticated-identity signing across environments (local dev, CI, containers), linked from the main docs. Motivated by the friction we hit configuring identity per-environment during the config-prune/identity epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A new doc `docs/identity-setup.md` gives step-by-step, placeholder-driven instructions + examples (create identity, git-email resolution, per-env signing-key delivery, verify, opt-in enforcement).\n- [ ] It contains NO secrets and NO deployment-specific infra details (generic, reusable by any client project) — verified by grep.\n- [ ] It is linked from the main documentation (docs/identity.md and the docs index).\n- [ ] Captures the hard-won lessons: materialize multi-line PEM to a 0600 file (not .env); set the signing-key env at CI job level (not cross-step); attribution is automatic via git-email but signing needs the key configured.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"71c41592-26e5-4ebf-b2c0-01e64688289f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["identity","docs"],"ticket_id":"3584-46b4-4f67-4988","ticket_type":"task","title":"Client-facing generic guide for setting up authenticated-identity signing","verify_commands":[]},